 "id": "ph_deep_barrows",
 "title": "Down the Deep Barrows",
 "kind": "hero",
 "seed": 5707,
 "intro": [
  "The dead keep fleeing upward, so the Regent goes down. Beneath the oldest barrows lies the Barrow Below, where the dead of the south have slept since before the Concord had a name. It is full of smoke.",
  "Something has dug into it from the east: tunnels still hot, walls scored with claws.",
  "Find the diggers, a brood under a chief called Garsh Emberclaw, and drive them out."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "ossric_woken"
   },
   "text": [
    "The diggers are Ashen: burrowers of the Host, tunnelling around the Lockstone through the land of the dead because the stone itself still holds.",
    "The dead did not wake because the world was warm. They woke because the Host was walking through their graves. Old King Ossric walks behind the Regent now, and his sleepers with him, and none of them will ever sleep again."
   ]
  },
